@startuml direct-rialto-handshake-stop-sequence
title Handshake: Stop() while an injector is blocked
skinparam shadowing false

participant "Control thread\nStop()" as CTL
participant "AampRialtoMediaSource" as SRC
participant "NeedDataHandshake" as HS
participant "Injector thread" as INJ
participant "IMediaPipeline" as PIPE

note over CTL
  Holds m_flushCallMutex, has waited for any flush
  to finish (WaitForFlushToComplete).
end note
CTL -> SRC : unblockInjection(pipeline, "Stop", newEos=false)
SRC -> HS : Unblock(false, previous)
note right of HS
  generation++, gateMode = DROPPED, eos = false.
  A request nobody owns is claimed and answered.
end note
HS -> INJ : cv.notify_all()
alt injector was in WaitForGate or WaitForRequest
  INJ -> HS : wakes: generation changed or DROPPED
  HS --> INJ : Abort (+ abandoned Claim if it owned a request)
  INJ -> PIPE : haveData(NO_AVAILABLE_SAMPLES, req)
  note right of INJ
    The injector uses the IMediaPipeline reference it took
    before Stop(), so the pipeline object is still alive.
    The call may fail once the pipeline is stopped: logged.
  end note
else injector was in WaitForAttach
  INJ -> HS : generation changed -> AttachWait::Aborted
  note right of INJ : sample discarded, "Attach did not complete (abort)"
end
CTL -> PIPE : stop()
CTL -> CTL : SetPipeline(nullptr), controller Reset, state machine onStop
note over CTL, INJ
  Sources stay DROPPED: later samples are discarded at once and
  never block a thread.  The next Configure() recreates the
  pipeline/sources (gated BLOCKED) or Flush() re-gates them.
  The AAMP side also calls UnblockTrackInjection() per track
  (StopTrackInjection(discard)) so the inject thread can be joined.
end note
@enduml
